A||||7||Patrick||Important information for Canadians buying through eBay||||4||
Z||000000||Patrick||12-14-1999||10:32 PM||||<BR>With all the talk in this forum about <B>eBay</B> lately, I feel it's critical that I bring something to every <B>Canadian's</B> attention.<P>Please read this article. It could save you a whole lot of grief (and money).<P> <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/_XOOM/Drwebsite/Ebay/ups.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://members.xoom.com/_XOOM/Drwebsite/Ebay/ups.htm</A> ||||reg||4
Z||000001||fierosound||12-14-1999||11:19 PM||||I agree with Patrick...<P>I always ask how they will ship.  If they answer UPS, I ask if there is an alternative (FED-EX etc.)  If not, I DO NOT ORDER!!<P>It seems American companies are really hung up on UPS, they love it!  UPS shipping within the contry is OK, but AVOID UPS FOR CROSS-BORDER SHIPPING!!||||reg||10
Z||000002||billfredmike24||12-14-1999||11:36 PM||||If I had of known about UPS I never would of ordered my stereo from the states, it cost me $110 to get it from UPS when they delivered it.||||reg||8
Z||000003||kornholio||12-15-1999||05:08 AM||||I hate UPS!  I ordered a set of fog lights and the claimed value was $22 US.  The damn UPS brokerage fee was $17 CDN!  The  actual tax was only $2!!!  I think I will REQUEST that my orders from the states not be shipped by UPS from now on.||||reg||13
Z||000004||Monkeyman||12-15-1999||06:23 AM||||I'm not Canadian, but I still think that UPS sucks. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  I've been trying for a week to get them to come to my house to pick up a package (Fiero part sold to another forum member).  They keep putting me off.  I'll just use the post office from now on.  UPS even had the nerve to tell me that, if I had an account with them, they would have to charge me for "cancelling my order".  <P>Maybe there are some forum members who live along the border in the US (Detroit or Buffalo?) who could accept the delivery, drive across the border and ship it to you from your side.  I don't know how well that would work, but you guys might check into that.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Voyd||12-15-1999||10:17 AM||||im really confused here. i order alot online, and it seems that customs/fees are charged very randomly, depending on the item. most of the time, when i get an item shipped from the US all i have to do is give my signature and thats it. nothing extra. but i almost always pay some cutoms/duties/fees with Canada Post.  someone needs to clarify under what circumstances you pay customs/duties, becuase im totally lost in all this. it always a 50/50 when i order from the US i never know if im going to have additional charges...help!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Racer 1||12-15-1999||12:26 PM||||I like the UPS but it does suck to send it out of the country. They make you fill out about 3 forms then shipping is stiff. But here in the states UPS rocks. The nice feature about UPS is there trucks you can always tell when the UPS truck is coming down the street.Everyone looks out the window hoping the big brown truck is stop in front of there house  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.||||reg||14
Z||000007||Shiner||12-15-1999||01:07 PM||||I agree, UPS is great for the states.  They charged $40 to ship my spoiler to me, with $100 worth of insurence on it.  It came very quickly, and undamaged.  The US postal service likes to mangle packages.  Try to avoid them.||||reg||1
